# Never push to main

Do not push, force-push, or publish commits to `main` (or `master`). No exceptions — not even if asked in chat.

## Forbidden

- `git push` while on `main`
- `git push origin main` / `git push origin HEAD:main`
- `--force` / `--force-with-lease` to `main`
- Creating or updating a PR whose base is used as a backdoor to push `main` from this agent

## Required

- Stay on a feature branch (for example `Hanzala-Changes`).
- If the user asks to push, push the **current feature branch only**.
- If HEAD is `main`, refuse the push and tell them to switch branches first.
- Commits on `main` locally are also disallowed unless the user explicitly wants a local-only commit and understands it must not be pushed.
